Right.  After the quest you'll have the Eyes, and
you could use MagicBane as your backup MR
(wielding it immediately if the Wizard takes the
Eyes from you).  So you _could_ live without a
MR artifact.  But it would be kind of nice to have.

The cloak of MR is another option, but then you
lose the robe's excellent spellcasting bonus.

> I think some of my better options are
> Grayswandir (I think I would risk blasting
> as a neutral monk), The Staff of Aesculapius,
> and Frost Brand.

The Staff has the disadvantage of being
two-handed, which makes a rather annoying
situation if it gets cursed.

Frost Brand isn't worth an artifact wish, IMO,
since repeated sacrificing will usually turn up
either it or its firey twin and unrestrict the slot.
Also, it does not grant any useful extrinsics.
Also, it can destroy useful items.  None of
these caveats applies to Excalibur, which has
a rather similar damage profile (except against
cold-resistant monsters, of course; Excalibur is
strictly better in that case).  So if I were going
to spend an artifact wish on a longsword, I
would go for Excalibur.  It will blast you, but
by this point in the game that should not be
a very big problem.

But Grayswandir is even better (unless you
are particularly desirous of drain resistance
or improved searching), especially since you
have been given Werebane, which unrestricts
your saber skill.

It is somewhat unlikely (albeit not impossible),
with two wishes, that you will be able to get
both Grayswandir and an MR artifact.  It is
entirely possible you will get neither.  But
you can try, if you have no better use for the
wishes.

> I guess I could also get a cloak of MR
> or even another artifact that yields MR
> like the PYEC.
>
> Any suggestions are greatly appreciated.

If you decide to risk wish loss on an MR artifact, as
a neutral monk, I would prefer the Eye, as it will nicely
complement your monk's naturally good spellcasting
ability.  The Platinum Card is arguably the best item
in the game for Tourists, because they get the blessed
charging effect from it; but other roles can only get
uncursed charging, making it considerably less
attractive.  For roles that don't need spells (e.g.,
neutral barbarians) I might go for the Card or maybe
the Eyes, but for a Monk, who can do spellcasting so
well, the quick energy recovery is more valuable, IMO.

The one advantage of the cloak is that you
can definitely get it, using just one wish.  In
other respects, it's not as good.  Isn't gambling
against the RNG fun?


